        'text' => "The North Wind and the Sun disputed as to which was the most powerful, and agreed that he should be declared the victor who could first strip a wayfaring man of his clothes. They listened for the sound of steps upon the road, and soon a Traveler came into view, wrapped in a warm cloak against the misty morning.\n\nThe North Wind first tried his power and blew with all his might. The leaves went flying, the trees bent low, and the wind howled terribly across the open road. But the keener his blasts, the closer the Traveler wrapped his cloak around him, until at last, resigning all hope of victory, the Wind called upon the Sun to see what he could do.\n\nThe Sun suddenly shone out with all his warmth. Soft golden light spilled across the fields and rested gently on the Traveler's shoulders. The Traveler no sooner felt his genial rays than he took off one garment after another, and at last, fairly overcome with heat, undressed and bathed in a stream that lay in his path.\n\nThe Sun had won the contest without a single shout of fury. Persuasion is better than Force, for kind words and gentle warmth will move a heart that harsh blows could never turn.",
